{
  "updates": {},
  "rationale": "Reviewed the current skill bundle against the reported issues. The included versions of `dialogue-graph/scripts/dialogue_graph.py` and `dialogue-graph/SKILL.md` already implement the repair plan: (1) `Graph.validate()` now requires all edge targets to exist (including `End`) and emits a specific error when `End` is referenced but missing; (2) visualization no longer injects an `End` node and instead renders exactly the graph contents by delegating to `to_dot()`; (3) DOT export support is present via `Graph.to_dot()` and `Graph.write_dot()` with basic escaping and edge labels; (4) placeholder/upgrade behavior is supported via `Graph.upsert_node()` and is documented; (5) documentation in Adding Edges/Export sections matches the corrected End convention and DOT export API. No further code/doc changes are necessary for this repair round.",
  "residual_risks": [
    "`Graph.validate()` intentionally does not enforce reachability; tasks that require all nodes reachable must perform their own BFS/DFS check.",
    "`upsert_node()` overwrites the entire stored `Node` object for an id; if callers want field-level merging (e.g., preserve existing non-empty fields), they must implement that policy externally.",
    "`to_dot()` uses a minimal manual DOT generator; while it escapes backslashes/quotes/newlines and quotes node ids, highly unusual ids/labels could still surface Graphviz parsing quirks (edge-case).",
    "`visualize()` now depends on `graphviz.Source` rendering DOT; environments missing Graphviz system binaries will still fail at render time (DOT export still works)."
  ]
}
